WEBVTT

00:00:20.650 --> 00:00:28.610
<b>LEGEND</b>

00:00:20.650 --> 00:00:28.610
<b>OF THE</b>

00:00:20.650 --> 00:00:28.610
<b>  GALACTIC HEROES</b>

00:01:53.210 --> 00:02:02.310
Chapter VIII

00:02:06.790 --> 00:02:10.180
Econia, the planet Yang
Wenli was assigned to...

00:02:10.180 --> 00:02:15.480
...is in the Thanatos System 480 light years from Planet Heinessen.

00:02:18.490 --> 00:02:27.380
Yang left Heinessen on October 31st, 
Space Year 788, arriving on November 9th.

00:02:31.410 --> 00:02:36.930
Since it was a rural area away from a main transportation hub, it took 9 days of travel.

00:02:46.430 --> 00:02:47.740
You must be
Lt. Commander Yang.

00:02:48.970 --> 00:02:50.800
I'm Lieutenant Patorichev.

00:02:50.800 --> 00:02:52.960
I'm here to pick
you up, Mr. Secretary.

00:02:54.930 --> 00:02:56.470
Um, thank you.

00:02:57.120 --> 00:02:58.060
Let me get your luggage.

00:02:59.160 --> 00:03:00.340
This way, please.

00:03:08.890 --> 00:03:14.790
To be honest, not many promising
officers are assigned here.

00:03:14.790 --> 00:03:16.460
Including myself.

00:03:16.910 --> 00:03:22.630
I never imagined that a famous person like
Lt. Commander Yang would ever come here.

00:03:22.630 --> 00:03:25.310
I'm not exactly
"promising," either.

00:03:25.310 --> 00:03:26.650
You're so humble.

00:03:26.650 --> 00:03:28.440
I wish that were the case.

00:03:28.440 --> 00:03:34.390
When you were assigned to Econia wasn't there a lady friend who cried and told you not to go ?

00:03:34.390 --> 00:03:35.190
There wasn't.

00:03:43.390 --> 00:03:44.050
Yang !

00:03:48.890 --> 00:03:49.630
Jessica !

00:03:51.500 --> 00:03:53.800
I'm glad I made it in time.

00:03:53.800 --> 00:03:56.880
My class ran long, so
I wasn't sure if I would.

00:03:56.880 --> 00:03:59.100
It's nice to see you.

00:03:59.100 --> 00:04:01.050
You didn't have to take
the trouble, though.

00:04:01.050 --> 00:04:03.920
If I didn't, Jean Robert
would be mad at me.

00:04:03.920 --> 00:04:07.800
He'd think that I was a coldhearted person who wouldn't tell his best friend goodbye.

00:04:08.490 --> 00:04:10.000
I'm also your...

00:04:12.960 --> 00:04:14.960
...friend, Yang.

00:04:20.280 --> 00:04:22.960
If you need anything,
just let me know.

00:04:22.960 --> 00:04:26.030
I'll make sure to send it to you,
no matter how long it may take.

00:04:26.030 --> 00:04:27.730
Just feel free.

00:04:27.730 --> 00:04:28.620
Thank you.

00:04:28.620 --> 00:04:29.930
I'm sure I'll take
you up on your offer.

00:04:31.090 --> 00:04:33.740
Oh, then, say
hello to Lap.

00:04:36.760 --> 00:04:39.030
He and I always seem
to miss each other...

00:04:39.030 --> 00:04:41.420
...and we end up asking you
to be the messenger, but...

00:04:41.790 --> 00:04:42.870
Take care.

00:04:42.870 --> 00:04:46.840
And come visit me sometime,
the two of you together.

00:05:12.780 --> 00:05:15.190
There are beautiful
women on Econia, too.

00:05:15.190 --> 00:05:18.580
Since Lt. Commander Yang is
high ranked, famous and young...

00:05:18.580 --> 00:05:20.440
...you'll be popular
among the female officers.

00:05:20.440 --> 00:05:21.830
I wonder.

00:05:21.830 --> 00:05:26.940
When I was on Heinessen, I thought my status was fine, but I was never popular.

00:05:29.310 --> 00:05:32.310
Come to think of it, this Lieutenant is actually older than me...

00:05:32.310 --> 00:05:36.100
...but I'm talking to him like he's junior to me without feeling awkward.

00:05:36.100 --> 00:05:40.380
I guess I've grown comfortable with the
customs of the organization called "the military."

00:05:46.840 --> 00:05:49.570
That's the capital of Econia.

00:05:51.190 --> 00:05:57.250
It's got the grandiose name of "Econiapolis,"
but the population is just over 100,000 people.

00:05:57.250 --> 00:05:59.680
According to the original plan, large-scale 
forestation should have been implemented...

00:05:59.680 --> 00:06:02.930
...and the population should have
expanded to over 1,000,000, but...

00:06:04.840 --> 00:06:07.140
I will take you on a
tour of the town later.

00:06:07.500 --> 00:06:09.600
That's very kind of you, but...

00:06:09.600 --> 00:06:12.140
...what are your official duties ?

00:06:12.140 --> 00:06:15.140
I'm supposed to be
the Assistant Secretary.

00:06:15.140 --> 00:06:21.150
It's my job to assist you, so please feel free to ask me anything.

00:06:21.150 --> 00:06:22.410
Thank you.

00:06:27.700 --> 00:06:30.090
The POW camp is
just ahead of here.

00:06:30.090 --> 00:06:32.380
There are 55,400 prisoners.

00:06:33.170 --> 00:06:38.290
They come to town for part-time jobs and
shopping; they live quite a carefree life.

00:06:39.710 --> 00:06:43.070
Econiapolis's economy can't survive without the existence of the POWs.

00:06:44.280 --> 00:06:47.960
In a way, the POW camp
is Econia's only industry.

00:07:02.000 --> 00:07:04.820
From here, it's the
property of the POW camp.

00:07:04.820 --> 00:07:08.930
Even though it is an internment camp,
and nighttime excursions are restricted...

00:07:08.930 --> 00:07:11.250
...POWs move around fairly
freely during the daytime.

00:07:11.790 --> 00:07:15.790
Even if they escape, there are
no other planets close by...

00:07:15.790 --> 00:07:19.650
...and the only habitable place on this planet is Econiapolis.

00:07:20.910 --> 00:07:23.980
But they really
are well treated.

00:07:23.980 --> 00:07:28.020
The Alliance has treated the
POWs well from the beginning...

00:07:28.020 --> 00:07:31.360
...to have them realize the virtues of a free democratic society.

00:07:31.360 --> 00:07:34.030
Recently, our budget
has tightened...

00:07:34.030 --> 00:07:36.910
...so we can't be as accommodating as we were in the past.

00:07:36.910 --> 00:07:40.210
Still, their treatment
isn't all that bad, either.

00:07:40.210 --> 00:07:44.800
But "POWs are treated better than the
Alliance soldiers" is a nasty joke, of course.

00:07:46.530 --> 00:07:47.360
We've arrived.

00:07:54.920 --> 00:07:56.670
I'm Lt. Commander Yang Wenli.

00:07:57.530 --> 00:07:58.500
Nice to meet you.

00:07:58.500 --> 00:08:01.240
I'm Captain Barnabee Costea.

00:08:03.340 --> 00:08:05.260
He's not as
authoritarian as I thought.

00:08:11.730 --> 00:08:13.670
March...Jasper ?

00:08:14.220 --> 00:08:15.630
Huh ?

00:08:15.830 --> 00:08:16.870
Yes, that's him.

00:08:16.870 --> 00:08:23.740
When I was young, I was at the 2nd Battle of Tiamat, under Admiral March Jasper.

00:08:25.790 --> 00:08:32.100
At that time, I was 16 years old, having just
finished professional school, a young soldier.

00:08:32.100 --> 00:08:37.380
I still remember the rush when Admiral Jasper talked to me for the first time.

00:08:37.760 --> 00:08:41.930
To meet a survivor of the 2nd Battle of Tiamat, in a place like this...

00:08:41.930 --> 00:08:46.120
...is this a coincidence,
or did someone arrange it ?

00:08:47.630 --> 00:08:51.280
What was Admiral
Bruce Ashbey like ?

00:08:51.280 --> 00:08:52.680
Let's see...

00:08:52.680 --> 00:08:54.980
...he was like a god.

00:08:55.690 --> 00:08:59.590
He couldn't be a target
of criticism or denouncement.

00:09:00.310 --> 00:09:04.060
He was an object of faith,
or something close to it.

00:09:04.060 --> 00:09:05.570
He was like that for
most people, I suppose.

00:09:07.070 --> 00:09:11.010
More importantly, there is
something I need to tell you.

00:09:11.010 --> 00:09:12.740
Yes, sir.
What is it ?

00:09:12.740 --> 00:09:17.200
In this camp, there
are 55,400 prisoners.

00:09:17.200 --> 00:09:17.930
Yes.

00:09:17.930 --> 00:09:21.930
On the other hand, our
soldiers number only 3,600.

00:09:22.730 --> 00:09:24.610
It seems like it.

00:09:24.610 --> 00:09:29.600
Can you confidently say that you can take on 15 prisoners with your bare hands ?

00:09:29.600 --> 00:09:30.890
Not at all.

00:09:30.890 --> 00:09:34.470
Then I suggest that you build
a good rapport with the prisoners.

00:09:37.630 --> 00:09:40.230
You don't have to act like
you're weak, but honestly...

00:09:40.230 --> 00:09:43.030
...if 55,400 people rebelled
against us at once...

00:09:43.030 --> 00:09:45.620
...there'd be no way to
quell them with 3,600 people.

00:09:45.620 --> 00:09:46.860
I suppose so.

00:09:46.860 --> 00:09:51.300
There is an autonomous organization among the prisoners.

00:09:51.300 --> 00:09:56.460
It's called the Self-Government Committee.
You'll have to work hard to gain their support.

00:09:56.460 --> 00:09:59.540
That's the wisest thing to do.

00:09:59.540 --> 00:10:01.150
Do you understand ?

00:10:01.150 --> 00:10:01.960
Yes, sir.

00:10:02.570 --> 00:10:06.800
The chair of the Self-Government
Committee is Captain Kefenhiller.

00:10:06.800 --> 00:10:08.680
You should meet him.

00:10:08.680 --> 00:10:14.800
"Greeting" is a weird way to put it, but it's sort of like a custom in this camp.

00:10:16.630 --> 00:10:19.940
"Custom" - that's an interesting
phrase the Superintendent used.

00:10:19.940 --> 00:10:23.290
In this camp, there aren't
any commanders, are there ?

00:10:23.290 --> 00:10:24.510
No, there aren't.

00:10:24.510 --> 00:10:26.500
There's one thing
I wonder about.

00:10:26.500 --> 00:10:30.490
In a camp like this, officers and enlisted tend to be separated from one another...

00:10:30.490 --> 00:10:35.930
...so enlisted or low-ranking officers are often inclined to claim authority.

00:10:35.930 --> 00:10:40.430
But in this camp, the highest-ranking officer
retains command just as he did previously ?

00:10:40.430 --> 00:10:42.540
I see you've done
your homework well.

00:10:42.540 --> 00:10:50.210
But it's not because of his high rank that old man Kefenhiller is so highly respected around here.

00:10:50.210 --> 00:10:51.480
Old man ?

00:10:51.480 --> 00:10:52.580
Yes.

00:10:52.580 --> 00:10:55.830
He's been here since he became a
prisoner after the 2nd Battle of Tiamat...

00:10:55.830 --> 00:10:59.680
He's the oldest prisoner here.

00:10:59.680 --> 00:11:01.460
43 years ?

00:11:02.340 --> 00:11:04.800
Once again, it's the
2nd Battle of Tiamat...

00:11:06.700 --> 00:11:10.670
From what I heard, even though he was
the successor to a Barony in the Empire...

00:11:10.670 --> 00:11:13.850
...and was a civilian officer on the promotional track in one of the local governments...

00:11:13.850 --> 00:11:19.440
...he threw away his position at the age of 25 and joined the military without rhyme or reason.

00:11:19.440 --> 00:11:22.210
In the military, too, he was an elite,
a candidate for a command position...

00:11:22.210 --> 00:11:24.210
...and had already been promoted to Captain by the time he was 28.

00:11:24.210 --> 00:11:27.230
Then he came to
the 2nd Battle of Tiamat.

00:11:27.230 --> 00:11:30.200
Though it was misfortune that
he became a prisoner in that battle...

00:11:30.200 --> 00:11:32.810
...he's stayed here ever
since for some reason...

00:11:32.810 --> 00:11:35.030
...even though he had many
opportunities to be released.

00:11:35.790 --> 00:11:38.230
He seems to have some personal 
circumstances of his own, but in any case...

00:11:38.230 --> 00:11:42.010
...being an Imperial aristocrat can be difficult at times, I presume.

00:11:42.010 --> 00:11:45.290
He was 28 years old when he
became a prisoner, which means...

00:11:49.060 --> 00:11:50.570
He's 71 now.

00:11:50.570 --> 00:11:53.160
He's sort of like the
chief of this camp.

00:11:53.160 --> 00:11:55.690
The present Superintendent
can't even stand up to him.

00:11:58.230 --> 00:11:59.870
I have another question.

00:11:59.870 --> 00:12:00.960
What is it ?

00:12:00.960 --> 00:12:03.130
Usually, once I greet
the Superintendent...

00:12:03.130 --> 00:12:05.670
...the next up should be the
Vice-Superintendent, shouldn't it ?

00:12:05.670 --> 00:12:08.700
And then the Chief Security Officer, since
he's the previously assigned Lt. Commander...

00:12:12.580 --> 00:12:17.070
For one thing, old man Kefenhiller
is a figure of that much importance...

00:12:17.070 --> 00:12:18.900
...and just between you and me...

00:12:18.900 --> 00:12:21.650
...that the Superintendent and Vice-Superintendent don't get along very well.

00:12:21.650 --> 00:12:23.780
The Vice-Superintendent
is on a promotion track...

00:12:23.780 --> 00:12:26.180
...so he's more competent
than the Superintendent...

00:12:26.180 --> 00:12:28.380
...in terms of administrative skills, but the
Vice-Superintendent is a rigid bureaucrat.

00:12:28.380 --> 00:12:32.950
On the other hand, the Superintendent worked his way up in the field, so he's not happy{with the Vice-Superintendent}.

00:12:32.950 --> 00:12:34.930
That's a common
issue, isn't it ?

00:12:34.930 --> 00:12:38.580
Moreover, the Vice-Superintendent does the night patrol every day.

00:12:38.580 --> 00:12:43.700
That's actually in accordance with the rules, but it hadn't been enforced at all here.

00:12:45.470 --> 00:12:48.240
To enforce it, and to demand that
the Superintendent do the same...

00:12:48.240 --> 00:12:52.130
...from the Superintendent's perspective,
a middle-rank administration officer...

00:12:52.130 --> 00:12:56.970
...was using the regulations to harass him.

00:12:57.580 --> 00:12:58.790
Oh, well.

00:12:58.790 --> 00:13:03.410
That's such a heart-cleansing relationship,
isn't it - with muddy water, I mean.

00:13:06.130 --> 00:13:12.370
In any case, you'll see the Vice-Superintendent
and Chief Security Officer at dinner.

00:13:12.370 --> 00:13:16.700
After all, your seat is next to the
Superintendent and Vice-Superintendent.

00:13:16.700 --> 00:13:17.780
Huh ?

00:13:17.780 --> 00:13:19.020
This way, please.

00:13:19.970 --> 00:13:22.020
They've got seat
assignments, too ?

00:13:22.710 --> 00:13:24.040
Oh, well...

00:13:32.680 --> 00:13:37.440
I am Kefenhiller,
Christoph von Kefenhiller.

00:13:37.440 --> 00:13:39.110
Please remember me.

00:13:39.110 --> 00:13:40.800
I'm pleased to make
your acquaintance.

00:13:41.510 --> 00:13:45.930
The pleasure is mutual,
Hero of El Facil.

00:13:45.930 --> 00:13:49.540
I never thought my infamy
would reach a place like this.

00:13:49.930 --> 00:13:51.980
How is it for you,
living here ?

00:13:51.980 --> 00:13:55.780
Well, if allowed to ask for more,
there's no limit to human desire...

00:13:55.780 --> 00:13:57.940
...so I sate myself
with what I have.

00:13:57.940 --> 00:14:00.220
Is there anything you'd like ?

00:14:00.220 --> 00:14:03.460
At my age, there aren't
many things I'd want.

00:14:03.830 --> 00:14:08.570
But there is a thing called intellectual curiosity - things I want to know.

00:14:08.570 --> 00:14:14.000
Ever since I came here, I've had a few topics that
I wanted to know more about and researched them.

00:14:15.090 --> 00:14:18.900
It was about Admiral Siegmeister's defection and the truth.

00:14:18.900 --> 00:14:21.300
I might ask you for some
files regarding that affair.

00:14:25.680 --> 00:14:30.520
Was Admiral Siegmeister
your acquaintance ?

00:14:30.520 --> 00:14:33.630
Your knowledge of history
seems to be lacking.

00:14:33.630 --> 00:14:36.500
The defection occurred
60 years ago.

00:14:36.500 --> 00:14:38.760
He and I are more than
one generation apart.

00:14:38.760 --> 00:14:40.400
I have no direct
connection to him.

00:14:41.290 --> 00:14:43.110
But that can't be helped.

00:14:43.110 --> 00:14:46.030
It's strange, but files
regarding Siegmeister...

00:14:46.030 --> 00:14:48.950
...are extremely rare in the Alliance, to which the Admiral defected.

00:14:50.710 --> 00:14:56.200
There is another thing I am interested in - the assassination of Admiral Michaelsen.

00:14:56.200 --> 00:14:59.880
This is something that
happened after I came here...

00:14:59.880 --> 00:15:04.330
...but Admiral Michaelsen
was an acquaintance of mine...

00:15:04.330 --> 00:15:07.200
...so I'd definitely like to
find out why he was killed.

00:15:08.230 --> 00:15:10.780
I am already over
70 years of age...

00:15:10.780 --> 00:15:14.830
...but I'd like to find out the truth
about these two affairs before I die.

00:15:14.830 --> 00:15:18.130
I've done a lot of research
and made some inferences...

00:15:18.130 --> 00:15:20.300
...but those are far
from being conclusive.

00:15:20.300 --> 00:15:23.420
Could you tell me about
them in a little more detail ?

00:15:23.420 --> 00:15:27.960
I'd like to assist you, and it would be nice to find out the truth behind these affairs...

00:15:27.960 --> 00:15:30.330
Are you sure
you want to know ?

00:15:31.330 --> 00:15:32.180
Yes.

00:15:34.570 --> 00:15:35.560
Well then...

00:15:35.560 --> 00:15:38.040
Are you going to tell
me the details, Captain ?

00:15:38.550 --> 00:15:43.530
Before you ask, you should do
some research on your own.

00:15:43.530 --> 00:15:47.080
You'll have lots of
free time here anyway.

00:15:47.080 --> 00:15:51.090
If you actually want to engage
in this, do some homework first.

00:15:54.140 --> 00:15:55.620
Then I'll do so.

00:15:56.500 --> 00:15:57.200
Huh ?

00:16:00.940 --> 00:16:03.410
What a great move you made,
to evade him like that.

00:16:03.410 --> 00:16:05.050
Huh ?

00:16:05.050 --> 00:16:08.080
That old man Kefenhiller does the
same thing and baffles everyone...

00:16:08.080 --> 00:16:12.210
...every time a new Superintendent or Secretary comes here.

00:16:12.210 --> 00:16:14.850
Does that mean
he was just lying ?

00:16:14.850 --> 00:16:19.500
I can't say so definitively, but it's probably better not to take him too seriously.

00:16:21.480 --> 00:16:23.310
Or is there something
that's bothering you ?

00:16:24.530 --> 00:16:28.580
This Lieutenant seems trustworthy - maybe I could tell him a little about my situation.

00:16:29.030 --> 00:16:29.970
To tell the truth...

00:16:38.210 --> 00:16:39.740
I see.

00:16:39.740 --> 00:16:43.500
It's certainly possible that someone
schemed to murder Admiral Ashbey.

00:16:44.470 --> 00:16:51.000
But it's inconceivable that the politicians at the time were behind the scheme, if I may say so.

00:16:51.000 --> 00:16:56.090
To kill Admiral Ashbey would be like tying a rope around your own neck.

00:16:56.090 --> 00:16:58.100
I see your point.

00:16:59.580 --> 00:17:02.270
But that's just
common sense.

00:17:02.270 --> 00:17:05.810
There might have been certain other circumstances surrounding the politicians at the time.

00:17:06.290 --> 00:17:10.070
But in any case, why are you so
preoccupied with that incident ?

00:17:10.070 --> 00:17:15.800
When you were assigned here your responsibility for that investigation ended, didn't it ?

00:17:16.710 --> 00:17:20.320
You're right - I don't
know how to put it, but...

00:17:20.320 --> 00:17:23.820
...unless I come to a conclusion
in this investigation...

00:17:23.820 --> 00:17:26.420
...I'll feel like I haven't
finished my "homework."

00:17:26.420 --> 00:17:27.740
"Homework"...

00:17:27.740 --> 00:17:29.190
I see.

00:17:29.190 --> 00:17:30.910
"Homework," huh ?

00:17:31.290 --> 00:17:33.180
That I understand.

00:17:33.180 --> 00:17:35.480
Until you finish it off,
you always feel uncomfortable.

00:17:36.870 --> 00:17:41.510
Besides, Secretary is just a title and doesn't have much to do...

00:17:41.510 --> 00:17:44.050
...so rather than just
killing time, it's better to...

00:17:44.050 --> 00:17:46.830
Yes, for a genius
like you, Lt. Commander...

00:17:46.830 --> 00:17:50.960
...it must be frustrating to be in a
do-nothing job in a place like this.

00:17:51.680 --> 00:17:54.340
But it'll be all over with
just a little more patience.

00:17:54.340 --> 00:17:56.680
As I said,
I'm not a genius...

00:17:56.680 --> 00:18:00.680
I have a discerning eye for talent.

00:18:00.680 --> 00:18:04.340
Eventually, the Lt. Commander will be
assigned to a much more important post.

00:18:04.340 --> 00:18:05.620
I guarantee it.

00:18:06.640 --> 00:18:08.640
I wonder.

00:18:09.450 --> 00:18:11.230
I don't have a particular
desire for that...

00:18:11.230 --> 00:18:15.300
...and as far as I'm concerned,
I wouldn't mind staying here till I retire.

00:18:15.300 --> 00:18:20.130
Here, there's no danger of me being killed,
and I don't have to kill anyone, either.

00:18:25.830 --> 00:18:29.780
I'll introduce you. Vice-Superintendent, Commander Jennings...

00:18:29.780 --> 00:18:32.290
...and Chief Security Officer,
Lt. Commander Bowy.

00:18:32.290 --> 00:18:34.290
Just ask for their
instruction in anything.

00:18:35.000 --> 00:18:36.440
I'm Yang Wenli.

00:18:36.440 --> 00:18:37.260
Pleased to meet you.

00:18:48.640 --> 00:18:51.070
I'm glad to make your
acquaintance, for half a year.

00:18:51.070 --> 00:18:54.340
If I have to stay here longer than six months, I'll re-introduce myself once again.

00:18:55.970 --> 00:18:56.560
Please come in.

00:18:59.010 --> 00:19:01.100
I'm First-Class
Soldier, Chan Tao.

00:19:01.100 --> 00:19:04.500
I'll be the
Lt. Commander's steward.

00:19:05.000 --> 00:19:06.130
Nice to meet you.

00:19:06.130 --> 00:19:09.780
I thought a steward
would be someone younger...

00:19:09.780 --> 00:19:12.160
I've always been an
officer's steward, for 35 years.

00:19:12.160 --> 00:19:17.190
Because of it, I haven't had to
shoot people or be shot by them.

00:19:17.780 --> 00:19:20.620
Um, there's one thing
I'd like to ask you, but...

00:19:20.620 --> 00:19:21.830
How can I help you ?

00:19:21.830 --> 00:19:25.270
If you can, I'd prefer it if the
room were a little more disorderly.

00:19:25.270 --> 00:19:29.990
That way, I don't know how to put it,
but I'll feel a little more at home...

00:19:29.990 --> 00:19:31.200
...does that sound weird ?

00:19:31.200 --> 00:19:36.530
It is...weird, but I've had
other superiors like that.

00:19:36.530 --> 00:19:40.380
Admiral Baron Wallice Warwick
was also like that, too.

00:19:40.380 --> 00:19:45.190
He was such an impressive person -
it was quite an honor to have served him.

00:19:45.190 --> 00:19:49.830
Hey now, it's
the 730 Mafia again.

00:19:49.830 --> 00:19:52.500
Admiral Warwick was an
excellent commander, wasn't he ?

00:19:53.480 --> 00:19:55.700
Yes, he was.

00:19:55.700 --> 00:20:00.530
He certainly deserved to be
called an excellent commander.

00:20:00.530 --> 00:20:06.050
As a person, too, he was distinguished,
and even to someone like me, he was kind.

00:20:10.360 --> 00:20:15.230
Um, yes, he was somewhat affected and 
acted like a god even though he wasn't one.

00:20:15.230 --> 00:20:18.580
But compared to his many virtues,
such a shortcoming pales in comparison.

00:20:20.710 --> 00:20:24.040
He had misfortunes in
his old age, didn't he ?

00:20:26.770 --> 00:20:32.420
As distinguished as he was, he couldn't influence everyone around him.

00:20:32.420 --> 00:20:35.230
I'm reluctant to
say vulgar things...

00:20:35.230 --> 00:20:38.910
...but there were some undesirable
characters around the Admiral at times.

00:20:39.670 --> 00:20:42.980
Does that mean Baron didn't
have an eye for character ?

00:20:42.980 --> 00:20:45.210
Would you like some coffee ?

00:20:45.210 --> 00:20:46.260
Thank you.

00:20:46.260 --> 00:20:49.620
But I prefer
tea to coffee.

00:20:49.620 --> 00:20:50.850
I understand.

00:21:04.700 --> 00:21:08.950
Baron Warwick, March Jasper...

00:21:09.690 --> 00:21:14.290
Each member of the 730 Mafia deserved to be called a great commander.

00:21:15.500 --> 00:21:17.830
The people who plotted
the death of Ashbey...

00:21:17.830 --> 00:21:21.130
...might have been counting
on them in some sense ?

00:21:21.130 --> 00:21:23.580
That after murdering Ashbey...

00:21:23.580 --> 00:21:27.500
...they could leave the rest of the 730 Mafia in charge of the Alliance's defense ?

00:21:27.500 --> 00:21:31.180
In truth, they actually became the nucleus of the Alliance Fleet afterwards...

00:21:31.180 --> 00:21:34.340
...but they never brought spectacular victories the way Ashbey did.

00:21:35.990 --> 00:21:40.230
As a result of the 2nd Battle of Tiamat,
the Empire was weakened considerably.

00:21:40.230 --> 00:21:42.830
All they managed to do was
merely prevent further invasion.

00:21:42.830 --> 00:21:44.920
Such an ill-natured
supposition can be made.

00:21:45.920 --> 00:21:47.830
But it's possible
that their existence...

00:21:47.830 --> 00:21:52.610
...might have been the psychological
crutch for those who plotted the murder.

00:22:00.360 --> 00:22:01.800
How noisy...

00:22:01.800 --> 00:22:05.310
...people who hinder our love and sleep will be cursed...

00:22:06.180 --> 00:22:06.710
Hello...

00:22:06.710 --> 00:22:08.310
...this is the
mortician's office...

00:22:10.690 --> 00:22:14.050
Lt. Commander Yang, please come to
the Central Control Room immediately.

00:22:14.050 --> 00:22:16.200
I would recommend that you
bring your gun with you.

00:22:17.330 --> 00:22:19.250
Was there an escape attempt ?

00:22:19.250 --> 00:22:21.070
You've got it exactly right.

00:22:22.830 --> 00:22:25.980
When I was little, I was told
that I had too much imagination.

00:22:25.980 --> 00:22:28.900
But there is a situation that the
 Lt. Commander didn't imagine.

00:22:28.900 --> 00:22:31.130
Like they're holding the
Superintendent as hostage ?

00:22:31.130 --> 00:22:31.850
You're close.

00:22:31.850 --> 00:22:32.700
It's the Vice Superintendent.

00:22:34.420 --> 00:22:35.560
I'll be right there.

00:22:37.260 --> 00:22:40.580
It's not to my liking, to say the least, but I guess they're making a conscientious effort...

00:22:40.580 --> 00:22:43.880
...not to bore the rookie
on his first night here.

00:22:44.920 --> 00:22:48.310
Yang thought of it as if it were someone else's issue because he himself...

00:22:48.310 --> 00:22:53.090
...had not had the time or opportunity to earn the resentment of the prisoners.

00:22:53.090 --> 00:22:57.370
But it would be proved later
that this belief was inaccurate.

00:22:57.370 --> 00:23:02.470
The incident was instigated
with Yang Wenli as the target.

00:22:59.700 --> 00:23:04.200
Planet POW Camp

